---
import Trang from '../../layouts/Trang.astro';
import TrangVanBan from '../../components/TrangVanBan.astro';
import { docNoiDung } from '../../lib/noi-dung';
const nd = await docNoiDung('en');
---
<Trang ngonNgu="en" noiDung={nd} duongDan="/en/privacy"
       tieuDe="Privacy — Beeftown"
       moTa="How Beeftown collects, uses and stores personal information.">
  <TrangVanBan hieu="Privacy" tieuDe="How Beeftown handles your information">

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send a table request or a job application, Beeftown stores your
        name, phone number, whatever else you choose to enter, and <strong>the IP
        address that request came from</strong>. The IP address is used to block
        spam and as evidence that you ticked the consent box; it is erased at the
        same time as the rest. If you attach a CV, the file is kept in a private
        store that only the owner and managers can open.</p>
      <p>The data is held in Supabase, a database service Beeftown rents. Apart
        from Supabase, nobody else reads it — except that messages you send us on
        Messenger go through Meta, and order messages you send us on Zalo go
        through Zalo (see the sections below).</p>

      <h2>When you browse this website</h2>
      <p>Beeftown uses Meta Pixel, a measurement tool from Meta (the company that
        owns Facebook and Instagram). When you open a page, Meta Pixel sends Meta
        the page you are viewing, the buttons you tap (calling, opening Zalo,
        opening Messenger, viewing a take-home order, sending a table request),
        your IP address, your browser type and a cookie ID. Beeftown uses these
        numbers to see how many people our Facebook and Instagram ads bring to the
        website, and to show Beeftown ads to people who have visited it.</p>
      <p>Beeftown <strong>does not send Meta</strong> your name, your phone number
        or anything you type into a form.</p>
      <p>Meta handles this data under Meta's own privacy policy, and may store it
        on servers outside Vietnam.</p>
      <p>If you do not want to be measured, turn on tracker blocking in your
        browser or use an ad blocker — the website still works fully. If you do not
        want ads based on your visit, turn off ads based on your activity off Meta
        in the ad preferences of your Facebook account.</p>

      <h2>When you message Beeftown on Messenger</h2>
      <p>Messages to the Beeftown Facebook Page go through Messenger, a Meta
        service; Meta handles those messages under Meta's own privacy policy.
        Beeftown uses an automated assistant on Messenger to take table requests,
        look up or cancel a booking, and answer questions about opening hours and
        the address.</p>
      <p>The assistant <strong>does not store the text of your messages</strong>.
        To remember which step you are on, it stores a one-way encrypted ID (it
        cannot be turned back into your Facebook account) together with what you
        are in the middle of entering — date, time, number of guests, name, phone
        number. This is <strong>deleted automatically after 30 days</strong> without
        a conversation. When you confirm, the table request is stored
        exactly as if you had booked on the website. Beeftown only counts events
        (messages, bookings, requests for staff) to check the assistant works —
        without names, phone numbers or message text. Beeftown does not use
        Messenger to send advertising.</p>
      <p>How to delete your data: see the <a href="/en/data-deletion">data deletion instructions</a>.</p>

      <h2>When you send a take-home order on Zalo</h2>
      <p>The Take home page <strong>does not store orders</strong> and does not
        ask for your name, phone number or address. When you tap to view your
        order, the packs you chose are sent to the page's server through the page
        address so it can write the order message; that address carries no
        personal information, and Beeftown does not store your order.</p>
      <p>You paste the message into the Beeftown chat on Zalo and tap Send
        yourself; that message goes through Zalo, and Zalo handles it under
        Zalo's own privacy policy. Beeftown reads the message in our Zalo OA
        inbox to confirm the order with you.</p>

      <h2>What we use it for</h2>
      <p>Booking details are used so the restaurant can call to confirm. Job
        applications are used to arrange a meeting. We only send news about dishes
        or events if you <strong>tick the box yourself</strong> — that box is never
        pre-ticked, and leaving it unticked does not affect your booking.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>Job applications are kept for <strong>six months</strong> from the date
        you apply, after which name, phone, email, IP address and CV file are
        erased. What remains — the date and the role applied for — is kept in a
        form that no longer identifies you, so the restaurant knows how many
        people applied in each round.</p>
      <p>Booking details are kept so the restaurant can see your history with us.
        You can ask us to delete them at any time.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your information, and you can opt out
        of messages at any time.{' '}
        {nd.email_lien_he
          ? <>Write to <a href={`mailto:${nd.email_lien_he}`}>{nd.email_lien_he}</a>.</>
          : <>Send your request by messaging the Beeftown Page on Messenger.</>}
      </p>

      <p class="nho">In line with Vietnam's Law on Personal Data Protection 2025
        (in force from 1 January 2026) and Decree 13/2023/ND-CP on personal data
        protection.</p>
  </TrangVanBan>
</Trang>
